// `chars()` and `split(separator:)` in a `foreach` are lowered to a borrowing iterator before the call checker runs,
// which let any label through (`split(sep: …)` and `split(nonsense: …)` both ran). Their arguments are checked as
// every call's are; tests/string_split is the call as declared.
fn uint8 main() {
    string s = "a/b/c";
    isize n = 0;
    foreach (string piece in s.split()) { n = n + 1; }   // -> REJECT
    return 0;
}
